Feature: Newsroom story sequence coaching

  Rule: Explain the editorial ladder
    Scenario: Coach on new story creation
      Given the issue type is "story"
      When creating an issue
      Then warn "Newsroom stories advance one stage at a time: idea, assignment, research, report, editor select, copywriting, published."
      Then explain "Each stage has a markdown artifact in stories/<story-id>/. Kanbus refuses skip-ahead and missing files."
      Then suggest "Fill idea.md, then run: kbs update <story-id> --status assignment"

    Scenario: Coach while a story is still an idea
      Given the issue type is "story"
      Given the issue status is "idea"
      When updating an issue
      Then warn "Complete the idea artifact before chartering assignment."
      Then suggest "Fill idea.md, then advance to assignment."

    Scenario: Coach before copywriting
      Given the issue type is "story"
      Given the issue status is "editor_select"
      When updating an issue
      Then warn "Copywriting is reader-facing work."
      Then explain "It starts only after editor selection from the private report."
